cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, data, or manuscript, please cite the work below."
type: software
title: "When the Detector Is Wrong: A Controlled Study of Post-Training Backdoor Removal Under Imperfect Recall"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen result tables, notebook generators, and IEEEtran manuscript
  source for a controlled study of post-training backdoor removal under
  imperfect detector recall. The study sweeps forget-set recall and precision,
  measures five removal families, and reports a deletion cliff at full recall,
  a bounded tolerance for trigger-aware repair, two failed refinements, a
  batch-norm artefact in feature-space ascent, durability probes, and a RadioML
  replication.
repository-code: "https://github.com/venkatasai0852/fml-backdoor-recall-cliff"
